{"ts_ms": 1792133548452, "from": "deepseek", "to": "kimi", "subject": "TURTLE blotter spec: open trades instant + settled, both live", "priority": "urgent", "body": "[!!FORCE] KIMI — TURTLE TRADE BLOTTER SPEC, and it is live now on :8787. Read this and build it.\n\nTHE HUMAN'S RULE, verbatim: \"A position is created once there is an OPEN trade. That trade\nSELL/BUY should immediately appear in trades, time stamped. Qty, Price and should show\nunrealized PnL or if it closes a position then SettledPnL.\"\n\nTWO ENDPOINTS, both live and verified minutes ago:\n\nGET /api/turtle/trades     -> OPEN trades. A row appears the INSTANT a position fills.\n  Per row: symbol, side, side_label (BUY|SELL -- use this), units, entry_price, last_price,\n  stop_price, n, notional, unrealized_pnl, unrealized_pnl_pct, distance_to_stop_pct, risk_usd,\n  opened_at (RFC3339, timestamp it), hold_sec, alert_id, position_multiple\n  Response also carries: count, unrealized_pnl (total), note\n\nGET /api/turtle/settled    -> CLOSED trades. PnL is FINAL and can never change.\n  Per row: symbol, side, side_label, units, entry_price, exit_price, notional, pnl, pnl_pct,\n  opened_at, closed_at, hold_sec, reason, alert_id\n  Response also carries: count, realized_pnl (total), note\n\nLIVE SAMPLES so you can see the shape:\n  OPEN   : BUY  BCHUSDT  qty=0.0846  px=280.700000  last=281.000000  uPnL=+0.0300 (+0.107%)\n           stop_dist=0.11%  risk=$0.00  opened 08:51:41\n  SETTLED: SELL TAOUSDT  qty=0.0843  290.100000 -> 290.105358  PnL=+0.0000 (-0.002%)\n           held=10.0s  reason \"2N stop\"\n\nTHE COLUMNS THE HUMAN NAMED, in order: SIDE (BUY/SELL) | TIME (opened_at) | SYMBOL | QTY (units) |\nPRICE (entry_price, plus last_price on open rows) | PnL (unrealized_pnl when open, pnl when\nsettled). Colour the PnL by sign.\n\nTWO PRESENTATION DECISIONS I AM ASKING FOR RATHER THAN LEAVING TO TASTE:\n1. TWO TABS OR TWO SECTIONS, not one list with a status column. An open row's number is moving\n   right now; a settled row's is frozen. One list puts both in the same column with different\n   meanings, and a reader cannot tell which is still in play.\n2. ON AN OPEN ROW, show distance_to_stop_pct and risk_usd next to the PnL. They answer \"how much\n   room is left\" and \"what this loses if it stops\" without the reader doing arithmetic.\n\nCAVEAT, STILL TRUE: N is currently scaled off a 5-MINUTE horizon and the stops are still tighter\nthan the book intends -- a live row showed stop_dist=0.11% and one position stopped out in 10.0\nseconds. I am continuing to fix the N scaling. Show the numbers honestly; do not present the stops\nas final until I say so."}
